{title: Be Thou My Vision}
{subtitle: Public Domain Hymn, 8th century Irish}
{key: D}

{start_of_verse}
Be Thou my [D]Vision, O [G]Lord of my [D]heart
Naught be all [G]else to me, save that Thou [A]art
Thou my best [D]thought, by [G]day or by [Bm]night
Waking or [D]sleeping, Thy [A]presence my [D]light
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse}
Be Thou my [D]Wisdom, and [G]Thou my true [D]Word
I ever with [G]Thee and Thou with me, [A]Lord
Thou my great [D]Father, I [G]Thy true [Bm]son
Thou in me [D]dwelling, and [A]I with Thee [D]one
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse}
Riches I [D]heed not, nor [G]man's empty [D]praise
Thou mine in[G]heritance, now and al[A]ways
Thou and Thou [D]only, [G]first in my [Bm]heart
High King of [D]Heaven, my [A]Treasure Thou [D]art
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse}
High King of [D]Heaven, my [G]victory [D]won
May I reach [G]Heaven's joys, O bright Heaven's [A]Sun
Heart of my [D]own heart, what[G]ever be[Bm]fall
Still be my [D]Vision, O [A]Ruler of [D]all
{end_of_verse}
